{
  "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
  "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, not just goods or merchandise. Goods, merchandise or other property. And does other property include any type of property?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Counsel, what do you do about the later -- the later statute that makes an exception to the exception?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "reference that case because we wanted to offer the Court a broad construction or make sure the Court was comfortable in knowing that we were comfortable with the \"other law enforcement officer\" phrase being read broadly to reach any -- you know, any loose tax or customs function."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask, following up on Justice Alito's question, has there ever been a debate in earlier stages in this litigation as to whether this was a detention?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Mr. Shanmugam, may I ask you -- this goes to your ambiguity point. May I ask you this question? If Congress wanted to cover all law officers, the only reason for mentioning the customs and excise people would be to make it very clear that they were within that category of all law enforcement officers, and I take it that's basically what you're saying."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You have a difference\nwith Mr. Andre on the extent to which other law\nenforcement officers assist customs and revenue agents.\nIn your brief you say that's a rare occurrence. And\nMr. Andre says oh no, it's quite common. So which is\nit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is that an officer is acting in a customs or tax capacity when the officer is actually acting in a revenue collecting capacity. And we believe that if the Court were to adopt that limitation, there really are no actual cases of which we are aware that would fall within that language. And indeed, it would cast some doubt on the meaning of the preceding phrase \"any officer of customs or excise\" because one might very well wonder whether under Petitioner's construction that phrase should also be limited to a revenue collecting capacity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But then you are saying,\ndon't read the statute as a whole. That argument, in\neffect, is saying isolate the phrase -- and we don't do\nthat."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Andre",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ANDRE: I'd like to first address the\ngovernment's resistance to making any concession that\nthe statute is ambiguous. First of all, if the\nstatutory language in this case was so clear, then so\nmust the statutory language in Circuit City. The\nlanguage had started out with the words \"any other,\" and\nclearly then were followed by words that have a very\nplain meaning out of context, \"any worker engaged in\ninterstate or foreign commerce.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Wouldn't they have IFP status?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Andre",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ANDRE: Even if a prisoner gets IFP status, they still have to pay the full filing fee. The IFP status only allows them to pay in installments. So it's debited off their account. So they still make a very real calculation when they decide whether to sue based on how much is at stake and how much is it going to cost me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Andre",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ANDRE: That's correct. There was $177 at stake and so perhaps my client shouldn't have sued because it didn't make a lot of sense, although he also did file the suit a couple years earlier when the filing fee was lower."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-9130",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "192c0093cd7c4cbd877b6d57a0128aed093b72b6ecb888d824f7f3051b327818",
      "evidence_id": "ev-192c0093cd7c-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Andre. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:08 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
